---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const pages = [
  {
    href: '/lab/m5-neural-accelerator/',
    tag: 'Hardware',
    title: 'The M5 Neural Accelerator',
    blurb:
      'Apple put a matrix engine in every GPU core. The speedup is real — and lopsided. Where it actually shows up in inference numbers, why decode barely moves, and how we confirmed our own MLX runs are served by the NA-aware engine.',
    started: '2026-08-22',
  },
  {
    href: '/lab/runtime-tracking/',
    tag: 'Transparency',
    title: 'Runtime Version Tracking',
    blurb:
      'A silent engine update between rounds is an invisible confound on every round-over-round comparison. Our policy: auto-update off, engine versions captured per run, deliberate review before any bump. Current engines and the changelog live here.',
    started: '2026-08-22',
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="Lab"
  description="The bench under the bench: instrumentation, hardware, and runtime findings that shape how GAUNTLET Bench measures."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Instrumentation &amp; controls</p>
    <h1>Lab</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The bench under the bench: instrumentation, hardware, and runtime findings that shape
      how we measure &mdash; published because a benchmark that doesn&rsquo;t control its own
      confounds is just vibes.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="lab-intro">
    Scores are only as trustworthy as the machinery that produced them. This section is the
    running record of what we&rsquo;ve learned about that machinery &mdash; the silicon, the
    inference engines, the metrics themselves &mdash; and the controls we&rsquo;ve put in place
    when a finding exposed a gap. Investigations stay open; entries get dated updates as the
    picture changes.
  </p>

  <div class="lab-grid">
    {pages.map((p) => (
      <a class="lab-card" href={p.href}>
        <span class="lab-tag">{p.tag}</span>
        <h2>{p.title}</h2>
        <p>{p.blurb}</p>
        <span class="lab-meta">Ongoing &middot; started {p.started}</span>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p class="lab-more">
    More investigations will land here as they mature: memory-pressure telemetry during long
    runs, prompt-length-controlled TTFT baselines, and effort-setting sensitivity in reasoning
    models are all on the workbench.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .lab-intro {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 22px 0 0;
  }
  .lab-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 18px;
    margin: 30px 0 0;
  }
  .lab-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 20px 20px 16px;
    color: inherit;
    transition: border-color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .lab-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent-bright);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .lab-tag {
    align-self: flex-start;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-bright);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 3px 10px;
  }
  .lab-card h2 { font-size: 19px; margin: 4px 0 0; }
  .lab-card p { margin: 0; color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 14px; }
  .lab-meta {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 8px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .lab-meta::before { content: '\25B8 '; color: var(--green); }
  .lab-more {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 30px 0 40px;
  }
</style>
